src.exort — ExoRT v2 single RT bundle
=====================================

This is the v2.0.0 "one bundle to rule them all" radiative-transfer version,
built by `make exort` (executable: run/exort.exe).

Origin
------
src.exort = src.n84equiv (the 84-band grid) + NH3 and CO absorbers ported
forward from src.n68equiv (nspecies 6 -> 8). It supersedes both n68equiv and
n84equiv:

  * The 84-band grid is a strict superset of the 68-band grid. The runtime
    band optimizer (optimize_band_sw / optimize_band_lw in
    src.main/exo_init_ref.F90) condenses whichever grid is loaded, so the
    84-band input never costs more in the working RT loop than 68 did.
  * NH3/CO were only ever present in n68equiv; they are now part of the single
    bundle.

Gas species (nspecies = 8): H2O, CO2, CH4, C2H6, O3, O2, NH3, CO.

Data layout (v2)
----------------
All eight gases read 84-band, HITRAN-2024 k-files from the flat per-gas dirs
introduced in the v2 data reorg (the legacy data/kdist/n68<gas>/ tree is gone):

  data/kdist/{h2o,co2,ch4,c2h6,nh3,co}/  n84_8gpt_<gas>_hitran24/2024_..._grrtm.nc
  data/kdist/{o2,o3}/                     n84_8gpt_<gas>_hitran20_..._grrtm.nc  (HITRAN-2020)

Stellar spectra read from data/stellar/ (renamed from data/solar/ in v2).
CIA (data/cia/n84equiv/) and continuum (data/continuum/) are unchanged.

Files
-----
radgrid.F90, kabs.F90, model_specific.F90, initialize_rad_mod_1D.F90,
initialize_rad_mod_cam.F90  — carry the NH3/CO additions (the "add a gas" pattern).
calc_opd_mod.F90            — taken from n68equiv (band-agnostic; band dims flow
                              from `use radgrid`, so it is correct on the 84 grid).
rad_interp_mod.F90          — identical across n68/n84 (whitespace-only diff).
cloud.F90, spectral_output_cam.F90 — n84 versions (gas-agnostic / 84-band addfld).

See REFACTOR_PLAN.md (Stage B) for the merge rationale and the per-file diff.
